comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T13:18:19.979Z",codex-agent,"Design: check active nonterminal lanes before claiming. Default start returns structured warnings naming lane and both paths; strict refuses before claim/worktree publication."
  "2026-10-16T13:26:26.111Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only startLane from the base branch made the strict regression fail with Missing expected rejection; focused test exited 1 (0 pass, 1 fail). Restored implementation. Source imports require no dist rebuild."
  "2026-10-16T13:44:05.193Z",codex-agent,"Full SDK reads materialize files even when empty; removed the redundant fallback from overlap preflight. All 93 tests passed before the stronger watch synchronization check exposed a fixture race, now corrected. Thresholds remain four dimensions at 100 percent."
  "2026-10-16T13:57:30.536Z",codex-agent,"Final gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass normally and with CI=1, isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Each run: 93/93 tests plus 1/1 packed npm/native Bun acceptance, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 21 authored source files at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Statements/lines 1337/1337; functions 72/72; branches 601/601 for normal npm and 600/600 for the other runs. Identity, types, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, package allowlist, changelog and publish attestation pass. Three behavioural revert proofs are recorded. Publication remains maintainer-gated."
  "2026-10-16T15:30:53.243Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 design and revert proof: full reads in the pinned SDK materialize files=[] even for a stored document with no files field; standard SDK reads omit the collection. Centralized the unchanged (item.files ?? []) normalization in itemFootprint and reused it in readyCandidates, startLane and lanes. Four real-tracker CLI regressions create tasks without ever adding files, also hand-shape valid legacy documents without files, then invoke start --strict or next and verify the branch and claim. All four pass. Reverting only itemFootprint to item.files!.map makes all four fail with TypeError on the real standard SDK read (0 pass, 4 fail, exit 1). Restored the fallback; no SDK mocks or coverage exclusions. Tests import TypeScript sources, so no dist rebuild is needed."
  "2026-10-16T15:55:00.900Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 final validation: pm test pm-swarm-overlap --run --progress passed both linked commands (2/2 overlap/parser tests and 4/4 file-less SDK/legacy CLI cases). Normal and CI-like npm and Bun release checks each passed 97/97 suite tests plus 2/2 packed acceptance tests and all four coverage dimensions at 100 percent across 21 source files. Statements/lines are 1341/1341, functions 73/73, and branches 603/603 normally and 602/602 in CI-like runs. The defensive fallback remains present and measured. Revert proof is recorded above. Leaving status in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-16T15:55:37.054Z",codex-agent,"Coverage branch-count correction to the previous result: normal npm and normal Bun each measured 603/603; CI-like npm measured 602/602; CI-like Bun measured 603/603. All are 100 percent. Statements/lines remain 1341/1341 and functions 73/73 in every configuration. The earlier grouped CI-like branch count should be read with this correction."
